A||N||26||johnt671||What is Mobil 1 tri synthetic v Mobil 1||||1||
Z||000000||johnt671||12-10-2001||04:13 PM||||Want to go to Mobil 1 and saw they make a tri syn.  is it as good as and/or different from Mobil 1?  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||REDHOTT88||12-10-2001||04:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by johnt671:<BR><B>Want to go to Mobil 1 and saw they make a tri syn.  is it as good as and/or different from Mobil 1?  Thanks.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I've heard only good things about Mobil 1<BR>oil.  (especially here at the forum.) <P>I recently changed the oil in my Chevy truck and used the  Mobil 1 tri synthetic oil, seems to be O.K. so far. Starts good and runs cool.<P>I bought another 5 quarts to change my Fiero's oil too for the long winter storage. ($4.50 a quart!! ouch..)<P>Try going to Mobils website for more info.. I was going to do that myself!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Steve<BR><B>1988 Formula 2.8L</B> V6 5 speed <BR><FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> (Red and shiny all over!)</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||johnt671||12-10-2001||05:32 PM||||Good idea.  When to the web page.  Looks like they just changed the name a bit.  Haven't bought the stuff in years and was concerned that it was a bogus  syn. like Castrol makes.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Master_Sushi||12-10-2001||09:55 PM||||Mobil 1 is all I run in cars I care about. Its some of the best oil you can get. Also make sure to use a good filter like AC Delco, Bosch, K&N, ect.<P>I thought the Mobil 1 "tri synthetic" and Mobil 1 were the same. Just marketing.||||reg||14
Z||000004||artherd||12-11-2001||07:09 AM||||The 'Tri-synthetic' is the real deal.  Engines worth more than your house are insured at $4/qt  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Mobil also is making a 'blend' of syn and petrol oil, being sold under the Mobil 1 name.  Stay away.<P>Get the good stuff, if you care at all about your automobile.<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000005||mrfixit58||12-11-2001||07:48 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by REDHOTT88:<BR><B> "I bought another 5 quarts to change my Fiero's oil too for the long winter storage. ($4.50 a quart!! ouch..)"<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hummm... my V-6 only takes 4 quarts.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>Suncoast Fieros<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <P><B>JUST ADDED: </B>1988 GT w/ T-Tops, 5-Speed, and Performance Sound.||||reg||1
