Z||000007||Spiff||12-11-2001||11:57 AM||||Wal Mart...$18 for Mobil 1 (5 quart container) and $3 for filter.<BR>The joy of doing it my self. Only when its nice outside. In the winter time, its off to Wal Mart.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||REDHOTT88||12-11-2001||01:54 PM||||Just changed the oil in my Fiero with Mobil1 tri synthetic.  <P>I also used the $9.00 X2 Fram filter.. It's about twice as big as the stock Fiero filter. Looks nice too,, all silver! Only the BEST!!<P>------------------<BR>Steve<BR><B>1988 Formula 2.8L</B> V6 5 speed <BR><FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> (Red and shiny all over!)</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 12-11-2001).]||||reg||12
Z||000009||REDHOTT88||12-11-2001||01:59 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrfixit58:<BR><B> Hummm... my V-6 only takes 4 quarts.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Actually, to be technical, the V6 takes 4.5 Qts. (per GM)<P>I couldn't buy 1/2 quarts!!!<P><BR>||||reg||1
